{
  "comment": "The published AOSP build inputs each guest image is made from, pinned by build number and SHA-256, one entry per Android major and guest architecture (x86_64, or arm64 with no 32-bit ARM). Change a build number (and the hashes) to move to a newer build. A file with a url is not one of the build's own outputs but a source file at the frameworks/base commit the build was made from (base64 encoded by the source server, so fetch.sh decodes it before it checks the size and SHA-256): services.jar's ART profile, which the image compiles the edited services.jar with. Move its commit with the build. Each image the release workflow makes gets the next revision no release has (make-image.py --next-revision); revision and the version suffix here are the lowest it uses, and what a local make-image.py run names its image.",
